Underline any personal data in a sample prompt and rewrite it safely.","stem":"Personal data found:\nSafe rewrite:","autoMarked":false,"lookFor":"Identifies identifying details (name, address, photo, ID number) as personal data, and rewrites the prompt with the real name replaced by something like 'a student'. Watch for the misconception that typing in someone's details is fine as long as it helps - personal data may be stored or used to train systems.","frameworkRefs":[{"framework":"AIF","strand":"GE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·GE·G6·E"}]},{"id":"g6-main-w5-core-g6-m-w5-core-q3","type":"shortText","prompt":"Record each risk you find with its who and rule. Complete the table columns: Scenario | Risk family | Who is affected | Responsible-use rule.","stem":"Scenario | Risk family | Who is affected | Responsible-use rule","autoMarked":false,"lookFor":"Each row sorts the scenario into accuracy or safety/privacy, names a specific who for every risk, and states a matching rule. Emerging: two different, genuine risks with a specific who each and a rule that clearly reduces the named risk.","frameworkRefs":[{"framework":"AIF","strand":"GE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·GE·G6·E"}]},{"id":"g6-main-w5-core-g6-m-w5-core-q4","type":"shortText","prompt":"Name two genuine risks of using AI tools and one responsible-use rule that reduces one of them.","autoMarked":false,"lookFor":"Two genuinely different risks - e.g. incorrect output used as-is (accuracy) and entering personal data (safety/privacy) - plus one rule that matches one of them, such as 'never enter personal or identifying data into an AI tool'. Redirect vague 'it is bad' answers to a specific risk plus who it affects.","frameworkRefs":[{"framework":"AIF","strand":"GE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·GE·G6·E"}]},{"id":"g6-main-w5-core-g6-m-w5-core-q5","type":"shortText","prompt":"Write a class responsible-use charter of three rules, each matched to a specific risk it reduces.","autoMarked":false,"lookFor":"Three realistic rules, each explicitly paired with the risk it reduces rather than listed as general advice. Stretch: a scenario that involves both risk families at once, with the overlap explained.","frameworkRefs":[{"framework":"AIF","strand":"GE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·GE·G6·E"}]}]},"formative":{"targets":"Directly checks 'recognises basic risks (incorrect outputs, unsafe use)'","check":"Risk-spotting exit card: name two risks + one responsible-use rule","successCriteria":"Names two genuine risks, explains who is affected, and states a matching responsible-use rule.","evidence":"Risk-spotting card."}},"g6-main-w5-lab":{"id":"g6-main-w5-lab","number":10,"week":5,"track":"main","type":"lab","title":"Class AI Risk Audit (Lab)","summary":"Groups act as a class safety board, auditing an anonymised AI use-log against the rules, ranking the gaps on a likelihood-impact matrix, and proposing one rule to fix the top-priority risk.","duration":"45 minutes","strands":["GE"],"objectives":["Audit the class's own AI use against a responsible-use rule set and propose one improvement.","Rank risks by likelihood and impact on a simple risk matrix and choose which to mitigate first.","Write one responsible-use rule to close a gap found in the audit."],"sections":[{"type":"text","heading":"Class AI Risk Audit (Lab)","body":["Today your group becomes a class safety board. You will audit how AI has actually been used, rank the risks you find, and decide which one to fix first - then write the rule that fixes it."],"role":"intro"},{"type":"list","heading":"I can…","items":["I can audit our AI use against a rule set and find a gap.","I can place risks on a matrix by likelihood and impact.","I can propose one rule to reduce the highest-priority risk."],"role":"objectives"},{"type":"vocabulary","heading":"Words to know","terms":[{"term":"Audit","definition":"Checking real practice against a set of rules to find gaps."},{"term":"Likelihood","definition":"How often a risk could happen."},{"term":"Impact","definition":"How much harm a risk would cause."},{"term":"Mitigate","definition":"To reduce a risk, often by adding a rule."},{"term":"Gap","definition":"A place where practice does not meet the rule."}],"role":"vocabulary"},{"type":"text","heading":"Audit against the rules","body":["An [[audit]] compares what actually happened with what should happen. You read the anonymised class use-log and flag any entry that breaks or stretches a responsible-use rule.","The log is anonymised on purpose: you fix systems and habits, *never* blame a person."],"role":"explain"},{"type":"text","heading":"Rank, then rule","body":["Place each flagged risk on the matrix by its [[likelihood]] and [[impact]], then pick the highest-priority one.","Finally, write one realistic responsible-use rule that would close that gap - and be ready to pitch it for the class charter."],"role":"explain"},{"type":"activity","label":"Let's try it - hands-on","heading":"Let's try it - hands-on","body":["Audit the anonymised use-log, flag the gaps, plot the risks on the matrix, and propose one rule to fix the top-priority risk."],"items":["Read each log entry against the rule set.","Flag gaps and name the risk and who it affects.","Plot risks on the likelihood-impact matrix.","Circle the highest-priority risk.","Write and pitch one mitigation rule."],"role":"activity"},{"type":"list","heading":"Think about it","items":["Which risk surprised you as higher priority than expected?","How do you make a rule strong but still realistic?"],"role":"discuss"},{"type":"list","heading":"My reflection","items":["Write one change you will make to your own AI use after this audit.","Explain why anonymising the log matters."],"role":"reflect"}],"worksheet":{"title":"Week 5 - Lab - Worksheet | Class AI Risk Audit (Lab)","questions":[{"id":"g6-main-w5-lab-g6-m-w5-lab-q1","type":"shortText","prompt":"For each log entry, note whether it meets the rules and flag any gap.","stem":"Meets rules? Yes / No\nGap found:\nRisk and who:","autoMarked":false,"lookFor":"Finds a genuine gap - e.g. a demo prompt that included a student's name - and names both the risk (privacy exposure) and the who (that student). Watch for blame-focused answers: the log is anonymised, and audits fix systems, not people.","frameworkRefs":[{"framework":"AIF","strand":"GE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·GE·G6·E"}]},{"id":"g6-main-w5-lab-g6-m-w5-lab-q2","type":"shortText","prompt":"Explain why your top risk is highest priority and write a rule to fix it.","stem":"Top risk because ...\nMitigation rule:","autoMarked":false,"lookFor":"Priority justified by matrix position - the high-likelihood, high-impact risk (usually privacy) comes first, rather than 'fix everything at once'. The rule must be realistic and actually reduce the named risk, e.g. replace any real name with 'a student' before using a prompt.","frameworkRefs":[{"framework":"AIF","strand":"GE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·GE·G6·E"}]},{"id":"g6-main-w5-lab-g6-m-w5-lab-q3","type":"shortText","prompt":"Record each flagged risk with its matrix placement and priority. Complete the table columns: Log entry | Gap / risk | Likelihood | Impact | Priority.","stem":"Log entry | Gap / risk | Likelihood | Impact | Priority","autoMarked":false,"lookFor":"Risks placed sensibly on likelihood and impact with a justified priority order, each row tied back to a real log entry. Approaching: risks placed but priority weakly justified.","frameworkRefs":[{"framework":"AIF","strand":"GE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·GE·G6·E"}]},{"id":"g6-main-w5-lab-g6-m-w5-lab-q4","type":"shortText","prompt":"State the highest-priority risk your group found and the one rule you would add to reduce it.","autoMarked":false,"lookFor":"Names one genuine top-priority risk consistent with the group's matrix, plus one workable rule that reduces it. Emerging: a realistic rule that reduces the top risk.","frameworkRefs":[{"framework":"AIF","strand":"GE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·GE·G6·E"}]},{"id":"g6-main-w5-lab-g6-m-w5-lab-q5","type":"shortText","prompt":"Design a one-page class responsible-use charter that closes every gap your audit found, ordered by priority.","autoMarked":false,"lookFor":"Every flagged gap is covered by a rule, and the order follows the matrix. Stretch: justifies a near-tie placement and explains how a rule would move a risk down the matrix.","frameworkRefs":[{"framework":"AIF","strand":"GE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·GE·G6·E"}]}]},"formative":{"targets":"Directly checks 'recognises basic risks (incorrect outputs, unsafe use)'","check":"Completed audit sheet with a matrix-placed priority risk and a proposed mitigation rule","successCriteria":"Finds a genuine gap, places risks sensibly on the matrix, and proposes a realistic rule that reduces the top risk.","evidence":"Audit sheet and risk matrix photo."}},"g6-main-w6-core":{"id":"g6-main-w6-core","number":11,"week":6,"track":"main","type":"core","title":"Bringing the Strands Together","summary":"Students run one guided challenge through all four strands and explain how each link in the chain shaped the next.","duration":"45 minutes","strands":["CU","SD","CE","GE"],"objectives":["Complete a guided challenge combining the concept, a prompted solution, an output check and a risk check.","Explain how the system type and prompt shaped the output.","Identify one responsible-use choice made."],"sections":[{"type":"text","body":["This term you learned four skills one at a time. Today you discover they were never separate - they form one chain, from understanding the system to writing a prompt, checking the output, and using it responsibly. Put all four hats on at once."],"role":"intro"},{"type":"list","heading":"I can…","items":["I can complete a guided challenge that uses all four strands.","I can explain how the system type and prompt shaped the output.","I can name one responsible-use choice I made."],"role":"objectives"},{"type":"vocabulary","heading":"Words to know","terms":[{"term":"Integration","definition":"Connecting separate skills into one process."},{"term":"System type","definition":"Whether a system is rule-based or learning-based."},{"term":"Prompt","definition":"The instruction you give an AI tool to guide its output."},{"term":"Triage","definition":"Judging an output as correct, incorrect, or unclear."},{"term":"Risk check","definition":"Asking what could go wrong and choosing a responsible action."}],"role":"vocabulary"},{"type":"text","heading":"One connected chain","body":["The [[system type]] shapes what you can expect. The [[prompt]] shapes the output. The output needs a [[triage]]. And the whole process needs a [[risk check]].","Each strand feeds the next - miss one link and the chain weakens."],"role":"explain"},{"type":"text","heading":"Explain the links","body":["It is not enough to complete each step; you should be able to explain how one shaped the next.","For example: because the prompt was specific, the output stayed on task, which made triage easier and the risk lower."],"role":"explain"},{"type":"activity","label":"Let's try it - hands-on","heading":"Let's try it - hands-on","body":["Run one guided challenge through all four strands, then explain how the system and prompt shaped the output and name one responsible-use choice you made."],"items":["Name the system type behind the task.","Write or choose a clear prompt.","Triage the curated output.","Run a basic risk check and note a responsible-use choice.","Explain how the system and prompt shaped the output."],"role":"activity"},{"type":"list","heading":"Think about it","items":["Which strand was strongest in your work, and which needs practice?","How would a weaker prompt have changed the whole chain?"],"role":"discuss"},{"type":"list","heading":"My reflection","items":["Write which strand you will focus on before the signature solution.","Explain one link in the chain in your own words."],"role":"reflect"}],"worksheet":{"title":"Week 6 - Core - Worksheet | Bringing the Strands Together","questions":[{"id":"g6-main-w6-core-q1","type":"shortText","prompt":"Complete each of the four steps for the guided challenge.","stem":"System type:\nMy prompt:\nTriage verdict and reason:\nRisk check and choice:","lookFor":"All four steps recorded: a named system type (e.g. a learning system for a text summariser, contrasted with rule-based), a specific prompt, a triage verdict of correct / incorrect / unclear with a checkable reason, and a genuine risk-reduction choice such as keeping personal data out of the prompt.","autoMarked":false,"frameworkRefs":[{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CU","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CU·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"SD","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·SD·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CE·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"GE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·GE·G6·E"}]},{"id":"g6-main-w6-core-q2","type":"shortText","prompt":"Write two sentences linking system, prompt, and output.","stem":"Because the system was ...\nThe prompt made the output ... which means ...","lookFor":"Both stems completed so that system and prompt are clearly linked to the output - e.g. a specific prompt gave a focused, on-task summary while a vague one would drift. Approaching links only two strands; not yet treats the strands as separate.","autoMarked":false,"frameworkRefs":[{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CU","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CU·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"SD","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·SD·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CE·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"GE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·GE·G6·E"}]},{"id":"g6-main-w6-core-q3","type":"shortText","prompt":"Record your result for each strand.","stem":"Strand | What I did | Result | Link to next strand","lookFor":"One row per strand with the action taken, a result, and a link showing how each strand fed the next: system type shapes the prompt, the prompt shapes the output, the output demands a triage, and the whole process demands a responsible-use choice.","autoMarked":false,"frameworkRefs":[{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CU","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CU·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"SD","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·SD·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CE·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"GE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·GE·G6·E"}]},{"id":"g6-main-w6-core-q4","type":"shortText","prompt":"Explain how the system type and prompt shaped your output, and name one responsible-use choice you made.","stem":"","lookFor":"Connects system plus prompt to the output quality and names a genuine risk-reduction choice that was made during the task (e.g. no personal data in the prompt), not added afterwards.","autoMarked":false,"frameworkRefs":[{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CU","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CU·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"SD","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·SD·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CE·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"GE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·GE·G6·E"}]},{"id":"g6-main-w6-core-q5","type":"shortText","prompt":"Redesign the prompt to lower the risk further, and predict how the output and triage would change.","stem":"","lookFor":"Redesigned prompt targets the risk that was identified (e.g. removes personal data, asks for checkable statements) and the prediction explains how both the output and the risk would change - the stretch expectation for this lesson.","autoMarked":false,"frameworkRefs":[{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CU","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CU·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"SD","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·SD·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CE·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"GE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·GE·G6·E"}]}]},"formative":{"targets":"Integrates all Term-1 Emerging outcomes before the signature solution","check":"Guided integration task reviewed against project success criteria; forward feedback","successCriteria":"Connects system+prompt to output, triages the output, and names a risk-reduction choice.","evidence":"Integration task + feedback note."}},"g6-main-w6-lab":{"id":"g6-main-w6-lab","number":12,"week":6,"track":"main","type":"lab","title":"Integrated Build-and-Check (Lab)","summary":"Students run a full build-and-check task across four stations, record accuracy and risk verdicts, decide whether to use the output, and diagnose their weakest strand.","duration":"45 minutes","strands":["CU","SD","CE","GE"],"objectives":["Run a small integrated build-and-check task end-to-end and record the checks made.","Identify which strand most needs work before the signature solution.","Evaluate the final output for accuracy and risk before deciding to use it."],"sections":[{"type":"text","body":["This is your dress rehearsal. You will run a real task from start to finish - build it with a system and a prompt, then check it for accuracy and risk before deciding whether to use it. By the end you will know exactly which strand to sharpen before the signature solution."],"role":"intro"},{"type":"list","heading":"I can…","items":["I can run a build-and-check task through all four strands end-to-end.","I can record the accuracy and risk checks I made.","I can name which strand I most need to improve."],"role":"objectives"},{"type":"vocabulary","heading":"Words to know","terms":[{"term":"Build-and-check","definition":"Producing an AI solution and then testing it before use."},{"term":"Accuracy verdict","definition":"Whether the output is correct, incorrect, or unclear."},{"term":"Risk verdict","definition":"How risky the output is and what would reduce it."},{"term":"Mitigation","definition":"An action that reduces a risk."},{"term":"Weakest link","definition":"The strand most likely to fail under pressure."}],"role":"vocabulary"},{"type":"text","heading":"Build, then check","body":["Building means choosing a suitable system and designing a clear [[prompt]] to reach a useful output.","Checking means triaging that output for accuracy and running a risk assessment before you decide to use it. Building without checking just produces confident mistakes."],"role":"explain"},{"type":"text","heading":"Decide and diagnose","body":["Your final call is **use**, **do not use**, or **use-with-changes** - and you must justify it with your two verdicts.","Then diagnose your [[weakest link]]: the strand where your evidence was thinnest. That is your focus before the signature solution."],"role":"explain"},{"type":"activity","label":"Let's try it - hands-on","heading":"Let's try it - hands-on","body":["Run the four stations end-to-end. Build with a system and prompt, check for accuracy and risk, decide whether to use the output, and diagnose your weakest strand."],"items":["Name the system type and why it suits the task.","Design a clear, specific prompt.","Triage the curated output for accuracy.","Run a risk assessment and choose a mitigation.","Decide use / do not use / use-with-changes and diagnose your weakest strand."],"role":"activity"},{"type":"list","heading":"Think about it","items":["Did your accuracy verdict or your risk verdict decide your use decision?","Which strand was your weakest link, and how will you strengthen it?"],"role":"discuss"},{"type":"list","heading":"My reflection","items":["Write your focus strand and one action to improve it before the signature solution.","Explain why building without checking is risky."],"role":"reflect"}],"worksheet":{"title":"Week 6 - Lab - Worksheet | Integrated Build-and-Check (Lab)","questions":[{"id":"g6-main-w6-lab-q1","type":"shortText","prompt":"Record your evidence at each of the four stations.","stem":"System type + why:\nPrompt:\nAccuracy verdict + reason:\nRisk verdict + mitigation:","lookFor":"System choice justified by the task (e.g. a learning system that finds language patterns, suited because summarising needs pattern recognition rather than fixed rules), a specific prompt, an accuracy verdict with a reason that can be checked against the source, and a risk verdict whose mitigation matches the risk (e.g. main risk is using an unverified detail; mitigation is verify before use).","autoMarked":false,"frameworkRefs":[{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CU","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CU·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"SD","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·SD·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CE·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"GE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·GE·G6·E"}]},{"id":"g6-main-w6-lab-q2","type":"shortText","prompt":"Make your use decision and name your weakest strand with a reason.","stem":"Decision: use / do not use / use-with-changes because ...\nWeakest strand:\nAction to improve:","lookFor":"A justified decision that treats use-with-changes as a real third option rather than a yes/no, plus an honest and specific weakest-strand diagnosis justified by where the evidence was thinnest, with one concrete improvement action.","autoMarked":false,"frameworkRefs":[{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CU","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CU·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"SD","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·SD·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CE·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"GE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·GE·G6·E"}]},{"id":"g6-main-w6-lab-q3","type":"shortText","prompt":"Complete one row per station and finish with your decision.","stem":"Station / strand | Evidence produced | Verdict | Note for signature solution","lookFor":"All four stations completed with recorded evidence and a verdict for each, finishing with the use decision. Emerging completes all four strands with recorded evidence; approaching completes most stations with some evidence.","autoMarked":false,"frameworkRefs":[{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CU","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CU·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"SD","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·SD·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CE·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"GE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·GE·G6·E"}]},{"id":"g6-main-w6-lab-q4","type":"shortText","prompt":"State your use decision with a reason, and name the strand you most need to improve before the signature solution.","stem":"","lookFor":"The decision is tied back to the accuracy and risk verdicts rather than to how the output looks, and the named strand is specific enough to act on before the signature solution.","autoMarked":false,"frameworkRefs":[{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CU","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CU·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"SD","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·SD·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CE·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"GE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·GE·G6·E"}]},{"id":"g6-main-w6-lab-q5","type":"shortText","prompt":"Rewrite your prompt so the output would earn a lower risk verdict, and predict how the use decision would change.","stem":"","lookFor":"Rewritten prompt visibly reduces the risk named at station 4 and the prediction explains the shift in the use decision (e.g. from use-with-changes to use) - the stretch expectation, which may also include a written justification of the use-with-changes option.","autoMarked":false,"frameworkRefs":[{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CU","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CU·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"SD","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·SD·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CE·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"GE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·GE·G6·E"}]}]},"formative":{"targets":"Integrates all Term-1 Emerging outcomes end-to-end as a rehearsal for the signature solution","check":"Completed build-and-check record with accuracy verdict, risk verdict, use decision, and weakeststrand diagnosis","successCriteria":"Runs all four strands end-to-end, records both checks, makes a justified use decision, and names a weakest strand.","evidence":"Build-and-check record."}},"g6-main-w7-core":{"id":"g6-main-w7-core","number":13,"week":7,"track":"main","type":"core","title":"Signature Solution - Planning","summary":"Students plan a five-part signature solution - goal, prompt structure, inputs, evaluation method and risk plan - and take it through an approve-to-build gate.","duration":"45 minutes","strands":["CU","SD","CE","GE"],"objectives":["Plan a structured AI solution: state the goal, the prompt structure, and the check steps.","Identify the inputs/data and the output-evaluation method.","Describe one risk and how the plan reduces it."],"sections":[{"type":"text","body":["Today you become a designer, not just a prompter. Before anyone types a single word into an AI tool, you will plan a small solution with five parts that fit together: a goal, a prompt structure, inputs, a check, and a risk plan. A good plan is like a bridge design drawn before the first bolt is placed - it lets you find weak spots on paper, where fixing them is cheap."],"role":"intro"},{"type":"list","heading":"I can…","items":["I can state the goal of my solution in one clear sentence.","I can lay out a prompt structure with a role, a task, and one rule.","I can name the inputs my solution needs and how I will check the output.","I can describe one risk and one way my plan reduces it."],"role":"objectives"},{"type":"vocabulary","heading":"Words to know","terms":[{"term":"Signature solution","definition":"A small, reusable AI design with a clear goal and connected parts that solves one simple task."},{"term":"Prompt structure","definition":"The shape of a prompt: a role for the AI, a clear task, and at least one rule or limit."},{"term":"Input","definition":"The information a prompt works on, chosen to contain no personal or identifying data."},{"term":"Evaluation method","definition":"The agreed way you will judge whether an output is accurate."},{"term":"Risk mitigation","definition":"A design choice that lowers the chance or impact of something going wrong."}],"role":"vocabulary"},{"type":"text","heading":"From one prompt to a whole solution","body":["In Grade 5 you improved a single prompt. This term you design a solution: a set of parts that work together to do one simple job well.","The five parts are the goal, the [[prompt structure]], the inputs, the [[evaluation method]], and the risk plan. If any part is missing, the solution is harder to trust."],"role":"explain"},{"type":"text","heading":"Writing a prompt structure","body":["A [[prompt structure]] names a role ('You are a timetable helper'), a task ('list the three earliest buses'), and one rule ('if a time is missing, say so').","The role focuses the AI, the task says exactly what to do, and the rule keeps the output honest and easy to check."],"role":"explain"},{"type":"text","heading":"Checks and risks before you build","body":["An [[evaluation method]] says how you will judge accuracy, such as comparing the output to a known-correct answer key.","A risk plan names one thing that could go wrong, like a confident wrong answer, and one design choice that reduces it, like a 'say if unsure' rule plus a human check. Never put personal or identifying data into a prompt."],"role":"explain"},{"type":"activity","label":"Hands-on","heading":"Let's try it - hands-on","body":["You will now plan your own signature solution on the plan sheet. You will not log in to any tool; the teacher runs any AI on the board. Your job is to make the plan complete and safe."],"items":["Read your task card and write the goal in one clear sentence.","Fill the role-task-rule slots for your prompt structure.","List the inputs your prompt needs, checking there is no personal data.","Write your evaluation method and one risk with its mitigation.","Self-check against the five-part list, then submit for the approve-to-build gate."],"role":"activity"},{"type":"list","heading":"Think about it","items":["Which part of a plan is easiest to forget, and why does that matter?","How does a 'say if unsure' rule make an output safer to trust?"],"role":"discuss"},{"type":"list","heading":"My reflection","items":["Write the one part of your plan you are most confident about.","Write the one part you will strengthen before building next week."],"role":"reflect"}],"worksheet":{"title":"Week 7 - Core - Worksheet | Signature Solution - Planning","questions":[{"id":"g6-main-w7-core-q1","type":"shortText","autoMarked":false,"prompt":"Name the five parts: using your task card, complete each part of the plan in one line.","stem":"The goal is to ___.\nThe AI acts as a ___ (role).\nThe task is to ___.\nOne rule is ___.\nThe inputs are ___ (no personal data).\nI will check accuracy by ___.\nOne risk is ___; my plan reduces it by ___.","lookFor":"All five parts are present: a goal naming the task and who it helps, a role + task + one rule structure, inputs with no personal or identifying data, a checkable evaluation method (e.g. compare labelled items to a teacher answer key), and one risk with a mitigation that clearly reduces that named risk. Evaluation and risk are the parts most often left blank or thin.","frameworkRefs":[{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CU","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CU·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"SD","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·SD·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CE·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"GE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·GE·G6·E"}],"tierProbed":"emerging","evidenceType":"product"},{"id":"g6-main-w7-core-q2","type":"shortText","autoMarked":false,"prompt":"Spot the weak plan: read the two sample plans provided","stem":"The stronger plan is ___ because ___.","lookFor":"Chooses the complete plan and names a specific missing part - the evaluation method or the risk row - as the reason, rather than saying the plan is longer or neater. Structure beats size: a missing check is a hidden weak spot.","frameworkRefs":[{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CU","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CU·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"SD","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·SD·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CE·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"GE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·GE·G6·E"}],"tierProbed":"emerging","evidenceType":"product"},{"id":"g6-main-w7-core-q3","type":"shortText","autoMarked":false,"prompt":"My plan review record: fill one row for each of the five parts (plan part / what I wrote / ready? Y/N) and mark whether it is ready.","lookFor":"One row per part, each quoting what the student actually wrote plus an honest Y/N. Check the evaluation and risk rows hardest: a 'Y' there should sit beside a method that can really be checked and a mitigation tied to the named risk.","frameworkRefs":[{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CU","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CU·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"SD","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·SD·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CE·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"GE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·GE·G6·E"}],"tierProbed":"emerging","evidenceType":"product"},{"id":"g6-main-w7-core-q4","type":"shortText","autoMarked":false,"prompt":"Exit ticket: write your goal sentence and the one risk your plan reduces.","lookFor":"Goal is one clear sentence saying what the solution does and who it helps. The risk is realistic (e.g. a confident but wrong answer) and is one the plan genuinely reduces through its rule, check or human step.","frameworkRefs":[{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CU","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CU·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"SD","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·SD·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CE·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"GE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·GE·G6·E"}],"tierProbed":"emerging","evidenceType":"product"},{"id":"g6-main-w7-core-q5","type":"shortText","autoMarked":false,"prompt":"Challenge (stretch): add a second rule to your prompt structure and explain which kind of wrong answer it is designed to stop.","lookFor":"Writes a second rule that fits the same prompt structure and names the kind of wrong answer it blocks (e.g. a confident guess, a dropped item, an unclear label). The link between the rule and the error it stops is what to look for.","frameworkRefs":[{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CU","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CU·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"SD","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·SD·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CE·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"GE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·GE·G6·E"}],"tierProbed":"emerging","evidenceType":"product"}]},"formative":{"targets":"Checks planning of the signature solution against the Emerging project criteria","check":"Plan review against the project rubric (Emerging); approve-to-build gate","successCriteria":"Plan states goal, prompt structure, inputs, an evaluation method, and one risk mitigation.","evidence":"Approved plan sheet."}},"g6-main-w7-lab":{"id":"g6-main-w7-lab","number":14,"week":7,"track":"main","type":"lab","title":"Prototype and Pressure-Test the Plan (Lab)","summary":"Students prototype their approved plan on the board, break it on purpose with a tricky curated input, and design an if-then fallback branch that keeps a person in the loop.","duration":"45 minutes","strands":["CU","SD","CE","GE"],"objectives":["Prototype the prompt structure and pressure-test the plan against a tricky input.","Add a fallback branch for when the output fails a check.","Record what changed and why after the pressure test."],"sections":[{"type":"text","body":["A plan on paper looks tidy. Today you find out how it behaves under pressure. You will build a quick prototype, then throw your hardest inputs at it on purpose - the missing item, the messy note, the two-in-one line. When it stumbles, you will not hide the failure; you will design a fallback branch that catches it safely. Engineers stress-test bridges before people cross them. You will stress-test your solution before it is trusted."],"role":"intro"},{"type":"list","heading":"I can…","items":["I can run my prompt structure on a normal input and read the output.","I can pressure-test it with a tricky input and spot where it fails.","I can add a fallback branch that says what to do when a check fails.","I can record the change I made and the reason for it."],"role":"objectives"},{"type":"vocabulary","heading":"Words to know","terms":[{"term":"Prototype","definition":"A first working version built quickly to see how a design really behaves."},{"term":"Pressure test","definition":"Deliberately trying a tricky input to reveal a weak spot."},{"term":"Edge case","definition":"An unusual input at the edge of what a solution expects, like a missing or double value."},{"term":"Fallback branch","definition":"A planned 'if a check fails, then...' response that handles a failure safely."},{"term":"Error type","definition":"A label for what went wrong: wrong, unclear, or missing."}],"role":"vocabulary"},{"type":"text","heading":"Prototype first, judge second","body":["A [[prototype]] is a fast first version. Running it shows how your design behaves, not just how you hoped it would.","The teacher runs your prompt on the board with a normal curated input. You read the output and decide: did it meet the goal?"],"role":"explain"},{"type":"text","heading":"Design the fallback branch","body":["When a check fails, a good solution follows a [[fallback branch]] instead of giving a confident wrong answer.","Write it as 'If the check fails, then ___ and ask a person.' Keeping a human in the loop is part of responsible design.","Remember: only curated, made-up inputs - never real names or personal data."],"role":"explain"},{"type":"activity","label":"Hands-on","heading":"Let's try it - hands-on","body":["You will prototype your approved plan, pressure-test it, and add a fallback branch. The teacher runs the AI on the board; you do not log in. Log every run."],"items":["Copy your prompt structure into the prototype slot of your log.","Watch the normal-input run on the board and record whether it met the goal.","Pressure-test with a tricky curated input and record the error type.","Write your fallback branch as an if-then sentence that asks a person.","Log the one change you made and the reason it will help."],"role":"activity"},{"type":"list","heading":"Think about it","items":["Which tricky input broke the most prototypes, and why?","Why is a handled failure safer than a confident wrong answer?"],"role":"discuss"},{"type":"list","heading":"My reflection","items":["Write the weak spot your pressure test exposed.","Write how your fallback branch will handle it next week."],"role":"reflect"}],"worksheet":{"title":"Week 7 - Lab - Worksheet | Prototype and Pressure-Test the Plan (Lab)","questions":[{"id":"g6-main-w7-lab-q1","type":"shortText","autoMarked":false,"prompt":"Predict then test: before the board run, predict how your prompt will handle one tricky input. After the run, record what actually happened.","stem":"I predict the output will be ___.\nThe actual output was ___.\nThe error type was ___ (wrong / unclear / missing).","lookFor":"The prediction is written before the run and the actual output after it, and the error type is one of the three labels. A real pressure test exposes something - e.g. 'found: charger and a scarf' returning 'devices' only is a missing error, not a wrong one.","frameworkRefs":[{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CU","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CU·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"SD","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·SD·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CE·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"GE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·GE·G6·E"}],"tierProbed":"emerging","evidenceType":"product"},{"id":"g6-main-w7-lab-q2","type":"shortText","autoMarked":false,"prompt":"Write your fallback branch: turn your exposed failure into a safe fallback using the if-then frame","stem":"If ___ then ___ and ask a person.","lookFor":"The branch handles the failure the pressure test actually exposed and keeps a person in the loop (e.g. 'if a notice names two items, then label each one separately, and if still unclear label it other and ask a person'). A vague branch, or one that does not match the observed failure, is only approaching.","frameworkRefs":[{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CU","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CU·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"SD","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·SD·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CE·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"GE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·GE·G6·E"}],"tierProbed":"emerging","evidenceType":"product"},{"id":"g6-main-w7-lab-q3","type":"shortText","autoMarked":false,"prompt":"Prototype build/test log: record each run - the input used (curated), the output, whether it met the goal (Y/N), and the error type if any.","lookFor":"At least one normal run and one pressure test are logged, each with its curated input, the output, a Y/N against the goal, and a classified error type for any run that failed. Logs without an error type are returned.","frameworkRefs":[{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CU","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CU·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"SD","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·SD·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CE·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"GE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·GE·G6·E"}],"tierProbed":"emerging","evidenceType":"product"},{"id":"g6-main-w7-lab-q4","type":"shortText","autoMarked":false,"prompt":"Exit ticket: write the weak spot you found and the fallback branch you designed for it.","lookFor":"Names one specific weak spot from their own log, not a general worry, and gives a fallback branch that visibly answers that weak spot.","frameworkRefs":[{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CU","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CU·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"SD","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·SD·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CE·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"GE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·GE·G6·E"}],"tierProbed":"emerging","evidenceType":"product"},{"id":"g6-main-w7-lab-q5","type":"shortText","autoMarked":false,"prompt":"Challenge (stretch): design a second fallback for a different error type and say which failure is more likely and why.","lookFor":"A second branch aimed at a different error type (wrong / unclear / missing) from the first, plus a judgement about which failure is more likely with a reason drawn from the runs they logged.","frameworkRefs":[{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CU","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CU·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"SD","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·SD·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CE·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"GE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·GE·G6·E"}],"tierProbed":"emerging","evidenceType":"product"}]},"formative":{"targets":"Checks that the plan survives a tricky input and gains a fallback branch","check":"Build/test log review: one normal run, one pressure test, one fallback branch, one logged change","successCriteria":"Prototype is run, a tricky input exposes a weak spot, and a fallback branch plus a logged reason are added.","evidence":"Completed build/test log with fallback branch."}},"g6-main-w8-core":{"id":"g6-main-w8-core","number":15,"week":8,"track":"main","type":"core","title":"Signature Solution - Building","summary":"Students build their signature solution by following their approved plan, evaluate and flag every output, and log one evidence-based improvement as evaluate -> change -> result.","duration":"45 minutes","strands":["CU","SD","CE","GE"],"objectives":["Build the solution by following the plan and prompt structure.","Evaluate outputs for accuracy and flag any that are incorrect or unclear.","Make at least one improvement based on an output check.","Keep personal and identifying data out of every prompt and keep a person in the loop for anything flagged."],"sections":[{"type":"text","body":["Today you build for real. You will follow your approved plan, run your inputs, and look hard at every output - not just the ones that look right. When you find an answer that is wrong or unclear, you flag it, change one thing, and watch what happens. This is how real systems get better: one careful change, one honest result. Keep every prompt free of personal data, and keep a person in the loop for anything you flag."],"role":"intro"},{"type":"list","heading":"I can…","items":["I can build my solution by following my approved plan.","I can evaluate outputs and flag ones that are wrong or unclear.","I can make one improvement and explain what changed and why.","I can keep personal data out of every prompt."],"role":"objectives"},{"type":"vocabulary","heading":"Words to know","terms":[{"term":"Build","definition":"Turning your approved plan into a working solution by following it step by step."},{"term":"Evaluate","definition":"Judging an output against your check to decide if it is correct and clear."},{"term":"Flag","definition":"Marking an output that is wrong or unclear so it gets attention and a fix."},{"term":"Improvement","definition":"One deliberate change made in response to an evaluation."},{"term":"Iteration loop","definition":"The evaluate -> change -> result cycle that makes a solution better over time."}],"role":"vocabulary"},{"type":"text","heading":"Follow the plan, do not improvise","body":["Building means running your approved prompt structure on defined inputs, not inventing new prompts on the spot.","Record each output before you change anything. That way you can see what your solution really does."],"role":"explain"},{"type":"text","heading":"Evaluate, flag, improve","body":["Evaluate each output against your check: correct, unclear, or wrong. Flag anything that fails.","Then make one improvement and re-run. Record it as **evaluate -> change -> result** so the cause of the improvement is clear."],"role":"explain"},{"type":"activity","label":"Let's try it - hands-on","body":["You will build your solution from your approved plan, evaluate the outputs, flag errors, and log one improvement. The teacher runs the AI on the board; you do not log in."],"items":["Restate your goal and check on your log.","Run your prompt structure on defined curated inputs and record each output.","Evaluate each output and flag the wrong or unclear ones.","Make one improvement in response to a flag and re-run it.","Log the loop as evaluate -> change -> result."],"role":"activity"},{"type":"list","heading":"Think about it","items":["How did you tell a subtly wrong output from a correct one?","Why is one change at a time better than many at once?"],"role":"discuss"},{"type":"list","heading":"My reflection","items":["Write the one improvement you made and why.","Write what you would evaluate more carefully next time."],"role":"reflect"}],"worksheet":{"title":"Week 8 - Core - Worksheet | Signature Solution - Building","questions":[{"id":"g6-main-w8-core-q1","type":"shortText","autoMarked":false,"prompt":"Flag the errors: read the five curated outputs provided. Mark each correct, unclear, or wrong and flag the ones that fail the check.","stem":"Output ___ is ___ (correct / unclear / wrong) because ___.","lookFor":"Judges each output against the known-correct reference rather than a hunch, catches both seeded errors among the correct-looking rows, and gives a reason tied to the check (for example, 'other' for a tablet charger is wrong because it should be 'devices').","frameworkRefs":[{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CU","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CU·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"SD","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·SD·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CE·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"GE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·GE·G6·E"}],"evidenceType":"product","tierProbed":"emerging"},{"id":"g6-main-w8-core-q2","type":"shortText","autoMarked":false,"prompt":"Log one improvement: choose one flagged output and record your improvement using the loop frame.","stem":"Evaluate: ___.\nChange: ___.\nResult: ___.","lookFor":"One change only, made in response to a specific flag, with the observed result recorded - for example 'Evaluate: charger mislabelled. Change: added a devices examples rule. Result: charger now devices, accuracy up.' Cause and effect should be visible in the loop.","frameworkRefs":[{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CU","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CU·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"SD","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·SD·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CE·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"GE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·GE·G6·E"}],"evidenceType":"product","tierProbed":"emerging"},{"id":"g6-main-w8-core-q3","type":"shortText","autoMarked":false,"prompt":"Build and improvement log: record each output, your judgement, whether you flagged it, and the improvement you made. Use the columns Input (curated), Output, Judgement, Improvement made.","lookFor":"The build follows the approved plan and prompt structure with defined, curated inputs rather than improvised prompts; every row is evaluated and flagged rather than only the obvious ones; all inputs are free of personal or identifying data.","frameworkRefs":[{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CU","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CU·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"SD","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·SD·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CE·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"GE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·GE·G6·E"}],"evidenceType":"product","tierProbed":"emerging"},{"id":"g6-main-w8-core-q4","type":"shortText","autoMarked":false,"prompt":"Exit ticket: write your one improvement as evaluate -> change -> result.","lookFor":"All three parts of the loop are present and connected, showing the change was driven by an evaluation and that the result was actually observed, not assumed.","frameworkRefs":[{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CU","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CU·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"SD","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·SD·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CE·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"GE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·GE·G6·E"}],"evidenceType":"product","tierProbed":"emerging"},{"id":"g6-main-w8-core-q5","type":"shortText","autoMarked":false,"prompt":"Challenge (stretch): make a second improvement and use your log to say which change raised accuracy more, with evidence.","lookFor":"Compares the two changes using evidence from the log rather than impression, and recognises that one change at a time is what makes the comparison possible.","frameworkRefs":[{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CU","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CU·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"SD","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·SD·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CE·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"GE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·GE·G6·E"}],"evidenceType":"product","tierProbed":"emerging"}]},"formative":{"targets":"Monitors build against the plan; each student logs one evaluation-based improvement","check":"Build check-in against plan + one logged improvement ('evaluate -> change -> result')","successCriteria":"Solution follows the plan, outputs are evaluated, and one improvement is made and explained.","evidence":"Build progress + improvement log."}}}};
}

